## std.string — strings (re-export barrel).
##
## The `String` type's canonical home moved to `std.types` (see
## lib/std/types.zag) so it can be imported as:
##
##   import std.types.{String}
##
## This file keeps the legacy `std.string.{String}` path working for
## existing callers (docs, examples, and lib/std internal imports all
## use it) by re-exporting the type. The re-export is `pub import`,
## which the imports loop emits as `pub const String =
## @import("types.zig").String;` — visible across modules, so both
## paths bind to the SAME zig type.

pub import std.types.{String}
